    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.aggregate_in_degree - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.aggregate_in_degree.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.aggregate_in_degree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get aggregate value from indegree of nodes.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.aggregate_in_degree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get aggregate value from indegree of nodes.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.aggregate_in_degree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Get aggregate value from indegree of nodes.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet aggregate value from indegree of nodes.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L55065-L55195){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.aggregate_in_degree(\n    agg,\n    conditions=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Aggregate in-degree](../assets/graphs/aggregate-in-degree.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A five-node directed graph with each node's in-degree in a badge. Node C receives three arcs, drawn in the accent color, more than any other node. The card lists the in-degrees 1, 1, 3, 1, 1 and their max, 3.0.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nComputes a single aggregate statistic from the indegree values of all nodes in a directed\ngraph. Useful for summarizing the indegree distribution or analyzing filtered node subsets.\n\nEach node's in-degree is found with `get_in_degree()` (parallel edges each count, edge\nweights are ignored), the nodes are optionally filtered with `conditions=`, and the\nremaining values are reduced to one number. Typical questions it answers:\n\n- how many incoming links does a typical node get (`\"mean\"` or `\"median\"`)?\n- how popular is the most-referenced node (`\"max\"`)?\n- do nodes in one group receive more links than another (compare `\"mean\"` with\n  different `conditions=`)?\n\nAll nodes in the graph are considered; any node selection is ignored, so use\n`conditions=` to restrict the set. Because each in-degree is counted by scanning the\nedge list, the cost grows with nodes times edges, which can be slow on large graphs.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[agg]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Aggregation function to apply. Must be one of:\n\n    - `\"sum\"`: sum of all indegrees (equal to the number of edges when no\n      `conditions=` are given)\n    - `\"min\"`: minimum indegree\n    - `\"max\"`: maximum indegree\n    - `\"mean\"`: mean indegree\n    - `\"median\"`: median indegree (the mean of the two middle values when the number of\n      nodes is even)\n\n<code>[conditions]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[Callable]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Filter function that takes a node object and returns `True` to include the node in the\n    aggregation. If `None`, all nodes are included. The node object has `id`, `label`,\n    and `attributes` properties; `attributes` is a dictionary, or `None` for a node\n    without attributes, so a safe filter looks like\n    `lambda n: (n.attributes or {}).get(\"kind\") == \"gene\"`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The computed aggregate indegree value. Returns `0.0` if no nodes match the conditions.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is undirected or if `agg=` is not a valid aggregation function.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~aggregate_out_degree`) \n\n:   The same summary for out-degree.\n\n[](`~aggregate_degree`) \n\n:   The same summary for total degree; also works on undirected graphs.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nEvery edge has one target, so the in-degrees of a graph add up to its number of edges. In a\nrandom directed graph with 20 nodes and 35 edges, the mean in-degree is `35 / 20`, or\n`1.75`:\n\n::: {#336e509b .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph(directed=True).add_gnm_graph(20, 35, seed=23)\n\ngraph.aggregate_in_degree(\"sum\"), graph.aggregate_in_degree(\"mean\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(35.0, 1.75)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Where the money goes\n\nIn a month of payments between bank accounts, an account's in-degree is the number of\npayments it received. With `conditions=`, the mean is taken over one kind of account at a\ntime. The four businesses are paid 3 times each on average, the 14 people fewer than twice:\n\n::: {#64d7a5af .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments = ec.payments()\n\n{\n    kind: payments.aggregate_in_degree(\n        \"mean\", conditions=lambda n: n.attributes[\"kind\"] == kind\n    )\n    for kind in [\"business\", \"person\"]\n}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n{'business': 3.0, 'person': 1.6428571428571428}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe business average hides a wide spread. The Grocer is paid 8 times, the most of any\naccount, and Acme, the employer, never. Here the accounts are sized by the payments they\nreceived:\n\n::: {#c28c61ef .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nreceived = {v: payments.get_in_degree(v) for v in payments.get_node_ids()}\npayments.set_node_attrs(\"received\", received)\npayments.plot(\n    color_by=\"kind\", size_by=\"received\", label_by=\"label\", seed=3\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#